  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I tried to play after this new EAC update. Touching the sticks triggers the A button and my A buttons don't work at all. I'm using index controllers, and YES I made sure the controller settings are set to default both in SteamVR and in VRChat. Every time I touch the right stick it makes me jump and every time I touch the left stick it mutes my mic or toggles gestures, or toggles my quick menu depending on what I have the controller profile set to in VRChat. It detects my controllers as Index controllers, but it's like it thinks they're Vive ones despite that because touching the touchpad also makes me move around as if I was touching the stick. The game has never been broken like this ever, seems like EAC has only made things worse. I was looking forward to a meetup tonight but the game is unplayable now. If you don't fix this within days, I'm going to Chillout and I won't be coming back. Most of my friends are already considering moving because of the recent controversy, as if that wasn't enough, now the game is unplayable, so even if I *WANTED* to play, I can't.\nEdit: I use a Vive Pro 2 but I have never owned VIve controllers and this has never been an issue. Detection shouldn't be based on the headset *anyway*, because the headset is just a screen. And as said, it detects the controllers as Index controllers *in the VRChat settings*",
